    // Optimized per-diagonal DP kernel
    //
    // Instead of computing a single cell (i,j) per Halide call (which
    // incurs a lot of JIT/realize overhead), we compute an entire
    // diagonal j - i = d at once.
    //
    // For fixed d, all cells (i,j) with j - i = d are independent:
    // every dependency of (i,j) lies on a smaller diagonal. So we
    // can compute the diagonal in parallel and/or vectorized.
    //
    // We still drive the diagonal loop from C++, and we still read
    // from the current 'table' buffer and write the updated values
    // back to it on the host, so the DP semantics are identical to
    // the original algorithm.
    // ------------------------------------------------------------------

